# Self-Healing ENDED Session Cleanup — Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (if subagents available) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Eliminate unbounded PostCommit overhead from zombie ENDED sessions by eagerly condensing on session stop, force-condensing stale leftovers, and marking empty sessions as fully condensed.

**Architecture:** Three layered components. (1) Eager condense on session stop — pays condensation cost once at stop time via the existing `CondenseSessionByID` path. (2) Force-condense safety net in PostCommit — catches sessions where stop hook failed/crashed, gated by 1-hour `stalenessThreshold`. (3) Immediate FullyCondensed marking for empty ENDED sessions — trivial skip for sessions with no files and no new content.

**Tech Stack:** Go, go-git v6, existing `strategy.ManualCommitStrategy` and `session` packages.

**Branch:** Update existing PR #599 branch `perf/force-condense-ended-sessions` — rebase onto `main` first to pick up go-git v6, perf instrumentation, and other merged changes.

**Related:** PR #599, Issue #591, PR #556 (FullyCondensed), PR #586 (phantom carry-forward fix)

---

